  "result": "I've written the plan, but nothing is changed yet because plan mode is on. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode here, so please confirm the plan below and I'll make the edit.\n\n**Cause:** `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py` (lines 386-392) gives a subcommand context the parent's whole `default_map`. It should give it only the entry for the subcommand's own name. With `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` context gets the outer dict, so its `port` option never finds a default.\n\n**Fix:** change `default_map = parent.default_map` to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. A missing key then means no defaults for that subcommand. I'll also make sure a `Sentinel.UNSET` value counts as absent.\n\n**Also planned:**\n- Add a regression test in `tests/test_defaults.py` covering a subcommand, a nested group, and a missing key.\n- Add an entry to `CHANGES.md`.\n- Run the related tests and then the full suite.\n\n`docs/commands.md` already describes the nested-dict form, so it needs no change.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-abundant-mountain.md`.",
